/-!
# Common arguments for the A₆ and A₈ cases of 16.4.9

This interface supplies the actual permutation-coordinate construction
target, the singleton conjugate-component intersection (**), the ensuing
pair and triple product exclusions, Thompson transfer into the complement
of O²(G), and the final order-thirty obstruction in S₅.

The exceptional branches still require the marked product model, the
elementary subgroup generated by the source transpositions, and the
model-specific Sylow and fusion arguments. No nonemptiness theorem for Δ₀
is asserted by these common results alone.

The A₆ five-point set must be taken inside A; `SixSetCorrection` gives
explicit permutations explaining the erroneous printed definition inside T.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
proof of 16.4.9(2), printed p.1192.
-/
